// The indirection is one step, and a re-export of a re-export is what makes
// that a claim rather than a description. Resolving modules in the order they
// are numbered bound the outer `use` to the inner one before anything had
// resolved it -- to a `use` declaration, which has no parameters and no type,
// so the call through it was an arity error.
//
// Following the chain where it is found needs no ordering to be true.
import mid

pub use mid.helper

fn main() -> UInt8 {
    helper(1)
}
